    "_postman_id": "5868956b-ee3a-489e-87a0-7d8ee2525e9a",
    "name": "Conduit Auth Users API Tests",
    "description": "# Conduit API Tests\n\nThis collection contains automated tests for the **Conduit API** — a real-world blogging platform API. The tests cover user authentication and identity endpoints, validating both happy-path and negative/error scenarios.\n\n## Base URL\n\n`https://conduit-api.bondaracademy.com/api`\n\n## Authentication\n\nCollection-level Bearer token authentication is configured using the `{{user_token}}` environment variable. This token is automatically captured and stored by the **User Login** request and reused by subsequent authenticated requests.\n\n## Requests Overview\n\n| # | Method | Name | Endpoint | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | POST | User Login | `/users/login` | Authenticate a valid user and capture the token |\n| 2 | POST | User Login - invalid email input data | `/users/login` | Validate error handling for a malformed email |\n| 3 | POST | User Login - invalid password input data | `/users/login` | Validate error handling for an incorrect password |\n| 4 | GET | Get Current User | `/user` | Retrieve the authenticated user's profile |\n| 5 | GET | Get User - Invalid Token | `/user` | Validate error handling for an invalid Bearer token |\n\n## Test Coverage Summary\n\n- **Status code validation** — every request asserts the expected HTTP status code.\n    \n- **Response body validation** — response payloads are inspected for correct structure and field values.\n    \n- **Token lifecycle** — the login request extracts and stores `user_token` in the active environment for downstream requests.\n    \n- **Negative testing** — three requests specifically target error conditions (invalid email, invalid password, invalid token) to confirm the API returns appropriate error responses.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "3587464"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "User Login",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code: 200 - Login Success\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response have user token\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.user.token).to.not.be.undefined;",
              "    // save token",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"user_token\", responseData.user.token);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response time is acceptable\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Content-Type header is application/json\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"application/json\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response body has correct user object structure\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData).to.have.property(\"user\");",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.user).to.have.all.keys(\"email\", \"username\", \"bio\", \"image\", \"token\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"User email matches the login email\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.user.email).to.equal(\"banetest@gmail.com\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Token is a non-empty string\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.user.token).to.be.a(\"string\").and.to.have.length.above(0);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Username is a non-empty string\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.user.username).to.be.a(\"string\").and.to.have.length.above(0);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n    \"user\": {\n        \"email\": \"banetest@gmail.com\",\n        \"password\": \"Test123!\"\n    }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{conduit_base_url}}/users/login",
          "host": [
            "{{conduit_base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "users",
            "login"
          ]
        },
        "description": "## User Login\n\nAuthenticates a registered user against the Conduit API using their email and password credentials.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/users/login`\n\n### Request Body\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user\": {\n    \"email\": \"banetest@gmail.com\",\n    \"password\": \"Test123!\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### What is tested\n\n| Test | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| Status code: 200 - Login Success | Asserts the API returns HTTP 200, confirming a successful login. |\n| Response have user token | Asserts that `user.token` is present and not undefined in the response body. The token is then saved to the `user_token` environment variable for use by subsequent authenticated requests. |\n\n### Notes\n- This request must run **before** any authenticated requests (e.g. Get Current User) so that `{{user_token}}` is populated in the environment."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "User Login - invalid email input data",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code: 403 - Login Error\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response body contains error message\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody({",
              "        \"errors\": {",
              "        \"email or password\": [",
              "            \"is invalid\"",
              "        ]",
              "    }",
              "    })",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response time is acceptable\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Content-Type header is application/json\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"application/json\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response body has errors property\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData).to.have.property(\"errors\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Error message is an array with at least one item\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData.errors[\"email or password\"]).to.be.an(\"array\").and.to.have.length.above(0);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response does not contain a user token\", function () {",
              "    const responseData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(responseData).to.not.have.property(\"user\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n    \"user\": {\n        \"email\": \"x\",\n        \"password\": \"Test123!\"\n    }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "https://conduit-api.bondaracademy.com/api/users/login",
          "protocol": "https",
          "host": [
            "conduit-api",
            "bondaracademy",
            "com"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "users",
            "login"
          ]
