        "description": "## User Login - Invalid Password Input Data\n\nVerifies that the Conduit API correctly rejects a login attempt when the password is incorrect.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/users/login`\n\n### Request Body\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user\": {\n    \"email\": \"banetest@gmail.com\",\n    \"password\": \"x\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### What is tested\n\n| Test | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| Status code: 403 - Login Error | Asserts the API returns HTTP 403, indicating the credentials are rejected. |\n| Response body contains error message | Asserts the response body contains `{ \"errors\": { \"email or password\": [\"is invalid\"] } }`, confirming the API returns a consistent error regardless of which field is wrong. |\n\n### Notes\n- This is a **negative test**. The password value `\"x\"` is intentionally incorrect.\n- The API intentionally uses a generic `\"email or password\": [\"is invalid\"]` error message for both invalid email and invalid password cases, which is a security best practice to prevent user enumeration."
      },
      "response": []
